		{
			dependencies: ["5BE9EDB88D656840"]
			description: [
				"Combining &9Titanium Tetrachloride&r with &6Magnesium&r in an &3Electric Blast Furnace&r (approximating the Kroll process) will net you your first &6Titanium&r. "
				""
				"This process is a loop, and therefore will not cost you any resources (apart from &6Rutile&r) if you process it correctly."
				""
				"Unfortunately, it is super hot. You'll need to cool it in a &3Vacuum Freezer&r for it to be usable."
				""
				"If you haven't set one up yet or want to improve your setup, routing through AE is an alternative way to using Pipez, LaserIO, or GT pipes. Simply set a Tag Storage Bus on the input bus of the freezer, set it to 'forge:hot_ingots', and set it to a high priority. This will accept any new Hot Ingots entering your system, and eliminates the need for a network."
				""
				"It also removes the need for a separate pattern dedicated to cooling the hot ingots."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:hot_titanium_ingot"
			id: "15372CBC9F2EA9BC"
