		{
			dependencies: ["6FB3E3D9CA0F4B30"]
			description: [
				"&9Rubber&r has been sufficient for making cables so far, but you will soon discover that this basic type of rubber won't withstand more than &2Extreme Voltage&r. Higher quality rubber is necessary to properly insulate your wires."
				""
				"There are two better types of rubber, and you will eventually need to make both of them. &eThese can also be used for insulating lower voltage wires more efficiently, requiring less fluid&r!"
				""
				"Both &9Styrene-Butadiene Rubber (SBR)&r and &9Silicone Rubber (SiR)&r can wrap any Cable tier up to &3UV&r. However, SBR requires petrochemistry infrastructure you may not have yet, and is not mandatory until you are making late-game components. On the other hand, SiR can conveniently be made from chemicals you are already familiar with. By setting this up now, you won't have to change your wire coating material later!"
				""
				"To make Silicone Rubber, you will need to create &6Polydimethylsiloxane Dust&r in one of several ways, then mix it with &6Sulfur&r in a &3Chemical Reactor&r. You can then coat wires with it in an &3Assembler&r."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:silicone_rubber_bucket"
			id: "08B36E2C37C417E5"
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [
