		{
			dependencies: ["508452E1A3E09B56"]
			description: [
				"As you continue to progress, crafting times for more advanced &3Electric Blast Furnace&r recipes will continue to increase. More advanced coils increase the operating temperature so you can smelt more advanced materials, &2and they also grant energy efficiency bonuses and speed bonuses to overclocking.&r"
				""
				"Despite this, you'll still need to get your infrastructure for smelting, as well as power generation, up to par."
				""
				"You don't need to get all eight of these completed and running just yet, but plan to at some point in the future. Instead of upgrading existing EBFs, have them passively automating a stock of materials and build new EBFs with higher specifications for new materials."
				""
				"Please note that beyond this point not all multiblock quests will have a bill of materials attached. You will need to use &3EMI/JEI&r to determine the structure and hatch requirements."
			]
			id: "4CC612FF64877C60"
			rewards: [{
				id: "4724F2EF968F3DE2"
				item: "kubejs:moni_dollar"
				type: "item"
			}]
			size: 2.0d
			tasks: [{
				count: 8L
				id: "33621E89E0E8F0A0"
				item: "gtceu:electric_blast_furnace"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&2Blast Furnaces Galore"
			x: 7.0d
			y: -11.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5BC6DB754207D4A8"]
			description: [
				"&2Large Turbines are decently powerful in GTm. They are quite complex to run, but can generate lots of power when done well and scale very well.&r"
				""
				"[\"\",{\"text\":\"Right now, you can make the \"},{\"color\":\"gold\",\"underlined\":true,\"text\":\"Large Steam Turbine\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"15A5B4C632836306\"}},{\"text\":\" and \"},{\"color\":\"gold\",\"underlined\":true,\"text\":\"Large Gas Turbine\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"7D72B3FF808CE13C\"}},{\"text\":\". Once you get a \"},{\"color\":\"dark_aqua\",\"text\":\"Fusion Reactor\"},{\"text\":\" going, you can make the \"},{\"color\":\"gold\",\"underlined\":true,\"text\":\"Large Plasma Turbine\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"1405D08C6A87B3BB\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
				""
				"Each Large Turbine will need a &3Rotor Holder&r of the same or higher tier than the Large Turbine itself, and a &3Dynamo Hatch&r capable of handling the energy output. Each &3Rotor Holder&r tier above the Large Turbine &9doubles&r the energy production and adds 10%% to fuel efficiency."
				""
				"You will need a &aRotor&r to go into each &3Rotor Holder&r&r. The Rotor will grant multiplicative Power and Efficiency bonuses depending on its material. Each Rotor also has a Durability, which is the number of seconds it will last."
				""
				"&aExample: &r&6Large Gas Turbine&r, with &3HSS-E Rotor&r and &3IV Rotor Holder&r:"
				""
				"&aProduction:&r 4096 * 2.80 * 2=22938 EU/t (91752 RF/t)"
				"&aEfficiency:&r 1.40 * 1.10=154.0%%"
				"&aDurability:&r 205,600 s (57.1 h)"
				"You can run the &6Large Gas Turbine&r off &9LPG&r and &9Methane&r from &3Fluid Rigs&r, or &9Nitrobenzene&r from &6Wood&r."
				""
				"The best &6Large Steam Turbine&r fuel is a closely-guarded government secret."
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "gtceu:turbine_rotor"
				tag: {
					GT.PartStats: {
						Material: "neutronium"
					}
				}
			}
			id: "0F779BEEED8E67BB"
			size: 2.0d
			tasks: [{
				id: "5A291BDB06F2E56E"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&2Large Turbines"
			x: 9.0d
			y: -11.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2977E1AF13E42DCB"]
			description: [
				"&2Fluid Rigs will harvest fluids from underground fluid veins. Note that the fluid veins are simply simulated and don't exist in the world. &r"
				""
				"Shift-right-click while holding the &3Prospector's Scanner&r to set it to fluid mode, then right click it in order to see the type and amount of fluid underground and to check the depletion state of the vein. The first number represents the base amount of fluid extracted per second. You can also check the &eFluid Vein Information EMI&r page for information on where they spawn."
				""
				"In the &eOverworld&r, it can harvest: &9Oil, Light Oil, Heavy Oil, Raw Oil, Natural Gas&r"
				"&6Salt Water&r is available as well, but only in Ocean biomes."
				""
				"In the &eNether&r: &eLava, Natural Gas&r"
				""
				"On the &eMoon&r: &9Deuterium, Helium-3&r"
				""
				"In the &eVoid&r: &9Oil, Raw Oil&r"
				""
				"As Fluid Rigs work, they will deplete the vein under them, reducing their yields. When a vein is depleted, it still yields a small amount of its fluid. The first tier of Fluid Rig takes &9100,000 operations&r to deplete a vein. Higher tier Fluid Rigs harvest fluids far faster and deplete veins slower."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:mv_fluid_drilling_rig"
			id: "2F04FA8D3E15E375"
			rewards: [{
				id: "62433A6A37041DE1"
				item: "kubejs:moni_dollar"
