		{
			dependencies: ["785C6332FC7A07A5"]
			description: [
				"So far, you have been using &6Energy Hatches&r only capable of drawing 2 amps of power. In &5EV&r, you unlock your first hatches capable of drawing 4 and 16 amps, called 4A and 16A Energy Hatches."
				""
				"With these new hatches, there is an important distinction to make:\n\nThe &aMax EU/t&r of a machine is determined by the combined amperage of its hatches. It is used for determining overclocks and thus recipe speed."
				""
				"The &aMax Recipe Tier&r of a machine determines the tier of recipes that are able to be performed, and is derived from the number of the highest tier hatches present. At 1 hatch, it is the tier of that hatch, and at 2 it is the next tier up. "
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Some examples:\n- Using only a 16A &5EV&r hatch will allow for &dLuV&r speeds on recipes &5EV&r and below.\n- Using both a 2A and 16A &5EV&r hatch allows for &dLuV&r speeds on recipes &9IV&r and below.\n- Using two 16A &5EV&r hatches allows for &dLuV&r speeds on recipes &9IV&r and below."
				""
				"If you're not always using superconductors, keep in mind: depending on your hatch configuration and the recipes the machine runs, the room for cable loss may vary. &eThe margin for error is smallest when using two regular hatches or one multi-amp hatch.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:ev_energy_input_hatch_4a"
			id: "7BC6E67521545949"
			size: 1.5d
			tasks: [{
				id: "5517C58C7834BFDD"
				item: {
					Count: 1
					id: "itemfilters:and"
					tag: {
						items: [
							{
								Count: 1b
								id: "itemfilters:id_regex"
								tag: {
									value: "input_hatch_4a|input_hatch_16a"
								}
							}
							{
								Count: 1b
								id: "itemfilters:not"
								tag: {
									items: [{
										Count: 1b
										id: "itemfilters:id_regex"
										tag: {
											value: "uiv|uxv|opv"
										}
									}]
								}
							}
						]
					}
				}
				title: "Any 4A or 16A Energy Hatch"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Higher Amperage Hatches"
			x: 0.25d
			y: -1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["39FD6F1076559156"]
			description: [
				"The &3Power Substation&r is GregTech's native mass power storage solution."
				""
				"The structure can accept up to 18 layers of 3x3 &aLapotronic Capacitor&r blocks. GT batteries can hold &96x&r the EU their item counterparts can hold when crafted into a &aLapotronic Capacitor&r. The structure need not be made of all of the same tier blocks, but it must be full, so fill any empty space with &aEmpty Capacitor Blocks&r."
				""
				"Insert power through &6Energy Hatches&r and extract from &6Dynamo Hatches&r, each of any tier. The Power Substation can accept special &664A Substation Hatches&r, as well as &aLaser Hatches&r."
				""
				"The Power Substation will &cpassively lose 1%%&r of its total capacity every 24 (real-life) hours, up to 100,000 EU/t per capacitor block. This is equivalent to &95.8 billionths&r of its total capacity per tick, so this should not be a concern under regular operation."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: "gtceu:power_substation"
