		{
			dependencies: ["36B1B083B4FA439F"]
			description: [
				"At this point in your progression, it is recommended you switch to a &acentralized power layout&r."
				""
				"Going forward, generators will be multiblocks that reduce the need for spam, but take up significantly more space. To save on cable, These multiblock generators should be close to where you store your power."
				""
				"A main &3Power Substation&r (&3PSS&r) is the best option for that power storage as its storage capacity and I/O rates far surpass normal battery buffers. If you consistently add to and upgrade the capacitors and hatches, a single PSS should suffice for the rest of the pack."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"For distributing power from that storage to your machines, it is a good idea to set up a &aPower Spine&r: a central power line dedicated to carrying the bulk of the power exiting your storage. For now this can be a regular wire or cable, but starting in &9IV&r this should be switched to &6Laser Hatches&r paired with &6Laser Pipes&r."
				""
				"With power roughly near your target area, use superconductors or regular cables to feed it to the machines. At this point there are several good options: &6Platinum&r, &6Vanadium Gallium&r, and &6Uranium Rhodium Dinaquadide&r."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:empty_tier_i_battery"
			id: "6CFAAF68D4B10062"
			size: 2.0d
			tasks: [{
				id: "5AF8E611CFEF3599"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Centralized Power"
			x: -1.0d
			y: -11.0d
		}
