			x: -3.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4EC59BC9BCCB3C5D"]
			description: [
				"Now that you have access to &3GCYm multiblock machines&r, it's a good time to begin work on a more involved ore processing system with the help of multiblock machines' greater throughput."
				""
				"As mentioned in the last quest on this topic, Macerate -> Ore Wash -> Forge Hammer -> Centrifuge is a good starting point. However, you may have noticed this approach not giving you enough of a certain byproduct, or taking too long to process certain types of ore."
				""
				"For those kinds of issues, you can use filters to process certain types of ore in a different way, for example by using the &3Thermal Centrifuge&r or &3Sifter&r on some, but not all, ore types."
				""
				"&cBe warned: tag-based filtering can work against you here! You will need to be discerning in how much processing you do for each type of ore."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"To be more specific, you will want to strike a &ebalance&r between byproduct yields per ore and processing time."
				""
				"Too much processing will result in clogs and wasted time spent waiting on your ore processing to \"catch up\" to a recent mining trip or microminer mission."
				""
				"Too little processing will result in you sending extra microminer missions or going on additional mining trips just for ores' byproducts."
				""
				"Ultimately, &ethe best route to take for each ore type will depend on your base and playstyle.&r Good luck, and don't forget to revisit and revise your filters regularly as you continue to progress."
			]
